# ─── Coverage / test artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────
# ⛔ ANCHORED DELIBERATELY. A bare `coverage/` matches a directory of that name
# at ANY depth, and on 2026-09-04 it silently swallowed `withCoverage()`'s whole
# source tree (`packages/hub/src/with-audit/coverage/`) and its tests: every
# local gate passed against files on disk, `git status` reported clean, `git
# add -A` added nothing, and CI failed on a subpath whose factory "did not
# exist". Vitest writes coverage to a PROJECT ROOT, so name those and only
# those. `check-architecture.mjs`'s `sources-tracked` check now fails on any
# ignored file under a package's src/ or __tests__/, so this cannot recur
# silently for a differently-named directory either.
/coverage/
packages/*/coverage/
test-harnesses/*/coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov
.vitest-reports/

# ─── Pack artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# ─── OS junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
