/scratch/

# ─── Project metadata ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `.npmrc` is a common accidental-token surface (_authToken=...).
# `.changeset/` IS TRACKED (changed 2026-09-14). It was ignored so "release
# notes come through the workflow" — but the cost was measured twice in two
# days: a `changeset version` run deleted 8 pending changesets and `git
# restore` could not recover them, because git had never seen them; and the
# 0.x `major` guard in scripts/release/no-major-pre1.mjs cannot run in CI over
# files CI never receives. Tracking them makes release notes reviewable in the
# PR that earns them, recoverable like any other file, and visible to CI.
# `.npmrc` stays ignored — it is a real token surface, which `.changeset/` is not.
# `.github/` is ignored by default, but workflows are needed for CI —
# selectively allow `.github/workflows/`.
.npmrc
.github/*
!.github/workflows/
!.github/workflows/**

# ─── Local-only AI configs (not published) ─────────────────────────
CLAUDE.md

